# Response headers Netlify adds to the site (Netlify reads this file).

# Security headers for every file, including the "page not found" page shown
# at a mistyped address. The Content-Security-Policy lists the only places the
# pages may load things from: our own files, Google Fonts, the Instagram embeds
# and their script, the Google Maps embeds, and the inline styles the pages
# use. Anything else is blocked. If you add an outside embed, script, font or
# form (a video, a calendar, a donation widget), add its address here too, or
# it won't show. It was in test ("report only") mode until Oct 2026; a check of
# the live pages found nothing it would block.
/*
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://www.instagram.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data: https:; connect-src 'self'; frame-src https://www.google.com https://www.instagram.com; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'self'; manifest-src 'self'

# Caching. Browsers may keep photos and other images for a day. The
# stylesheet is linked as main.css?v=N and N changes with every edit, so it
# can be kept for a week. Scripts (js/) and content files (data/) have no
# version number, so they are left out on purpose: browsers re-check them on
# every visit, and edits show up right away.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400
/css/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800
